{"timestamp":"2026-07-22T11:09:40.074Z","type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"agent_message","message":"The universal proof exposed a backend-specific issue: the Haskell prover eagerly case-splits the concrete `iteVal` evaluator on an unknown list-length condition. I’m separating that evaluator into K’s concrete-only module—LLVM keeps executable behavior, while symbolic verification retains the conditional as a value that can be compared directly to the contract.","phase":"commentary","memory_citation":null}}
{"timestamp":"2026-07-22T11:09:40.075Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"message","id":"msg_01ef6dc52292a652016a60a4f2b1d08197b930b7703b5388d0","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"output_text","text":"The universal proof exposed a backend-specific issue: the Haskell prover eagerly case-splits the concrete `iteVal` evaluator on an unknown list-length condition. I’m separating that evaluator into K’s concrete-only module—LLVM keeps executable behavior, while symbolic verification retains the conditional as a value that can be compared directly to the contract."}],"phase":"commentary","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"019f897e-45d3-74e3-bd7e-534d1e4b8187"}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-07-22T11:09:42.877Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_01ef6dc52292a652016a60a4f40e748197addb5d627ad620e2","status":"completed","call_id":"call_7rxDuoMRbmoE60FcNDil6mUh","name":"exec","input":"const patch = \"*** Begin Patch\\n*** Update File: /work/semantic.k\\n@@\\n-module SEMANTIC\\n+module SEMANTIC-BASE\\n@@\\n-  rule iteVal(B, V, _) => V\\n-    requires B [concrete(B)]\\n-  rule iteVal(B, _, W) => W\\n-    requires notBool B [concrete(B)]\\n-\\n   // sorted(set(xs)): insertion sort with equality elimination.\\n@@\\n   rule itemAt(cons(_, IS), N) => itemAt(IS, N -Int 1)\\n     requires N >Int 0 [concrete]\\n endmodule\\n+\\n+// These equations are needed for concrete LLVM execution.  Omitting them\\n+// from the Haskell definition prevents an unknown Bool from being split into\\n+// speculative true/false branches; the symbolic iteVal is itself the value.\\n+module ITE-CONCRETE [concrete]\\n+  imports SEMANTIC-BASE\\n+\\n+  rule iteVal(true,  V, _) => V\\n+  rule iteVal(false, _, W) => W\\n+endmodule\\n+\\n+module SEMANTIC\\n+  imports SEMANTIC-BASE\\n+  imports ITE-CONCRETE\\n+endmodule\\n*** End Patch\";\ntext(await tools.apply_patch(patch));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"019f897e-45d3-74e3-bd7e-534d1e4b8187"}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-07-22T11:09:42.895Z","type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"patch_apply_end","call_id":"exec-3f0535dd-0356-410d-b07a-e0844f1059a0","turn_id":"019f897e-45d3-74e3-bd7e-534d1e4b8187","stdout":"Success. Updated the following files:\nM /work/semantic.k\n","stderr":"","success":true,"changes":{"/work/semantic.k":{"type":"update","unified_diff":"@@ -27,3 +27,3 @@\n \n-module SEMANTIC\n+module SEMANTIC-BASE\n   imports MPY-SYNTAX\n@@ -121,7 +121,2 @@\n \n-  rule iteVal(B, V, _) => V\n-    requires B [concrete(B)]\n-  rule iteVal(B, _, W) => W\n-    requires notBool B [concrete(B)]\n-\n   // sorted(set(xs)): insertion sort with equality elimination.\n@@ -147 +142,16 @@\n endmodule\n+\n+// These equations are needed for concrete LLVM execution.  Omitting them\n+// from the Haskell definition prevents an unknown Bool from being split into\n+// speculative true/false branches; the symbolic iteVal is itself the value.\n+module ITE-CONCRETE [concrete]\n+  imports SEMANTIC-BASE\n+\n+  rule iteVal(true,  V, _) => V\n+  rule iteVal(false, _, W) => W\n+endmodule\n+\n+module SEMANTIC\n+  imports SEMANTIC-BASE\n+  imports ITE-CONCRETE\n+endmodule\n","move_path":null}},"status":"completed"}}
